          "**Predominance of Small-Scale Industries:** Large industries formed a small segment of the economy; most workers worked in small workshops and household units. Handloom production actually expanded in the 20th century due to technological improvements, especially the adoption of the **Fly Shuttle** (a mechanical device that speeded weaving, increased productivity, and reduced labour demand).",
          "**Marketing Goods:** Advertisements created new consumer desires. Manchester goods carried cloth labels with 'MADE IN MANCHESTER' and illustrations of **Indian gods and goddesses** (Krishna, Saraswati) to give divine approval to foreign products. Calendars were printed and hung in shops and poor homes. Indian manufacturers used nationalist messages: *'If you care for the nation then buy products that are made in India.'*"
