          "India is one of the world's richest countries in terms of biological diversity: possesses nearly **8% of the total number of species** in the world (estimated to be 1.6 million). Over 81,000 species of fauna and 47,000 species of flora (15,000 flowering plants endemic to India).",
          "At least 10% of India's recorded wild flora and 20% of its mammals are on the threatened list. Many are on the verge of extinction, like the **cheetah** (declared extinct in India in **1952**), pink-headed duck, mountain quail, forest spotted owlet, and plants like *Madhuca insignis* (wild mahua) and *Hubbardia heptaneuron* (grass species)."
