          "**Causes of Water Scarcity:**",
          "(1) **Large and Growing Population:** Higher demand for drinking, domestic use, and agricultural food production.",
          "(2) **Intensive Agriculture & Tube-wells:** Post-Green Revolution farming relies on high-water-consuming crops (rice, sugarcane) and individual tube-wells, causing groundwater tables to plummet.",
          "(3) **Industrialisation & Urbanisation:** Industries consume huge volumes of water and require hydroelectricity. Urban housing complexes have their own groundwater pumping devices.",
          "(4) **Bad Quality / Pollution:** Even where water is amply available, it is polluted by domestic and industrial wastes, chemicals, pesticides, and fertilizers, making it hazardous for human use."
