          "(2) **Khadins & Johads:** In arid and semi-arid regions of Rajasthan, agricultural fields were converted into rain-fed storage structures that allowed water to stand and moisten the soil (**Khadins** in Jaisalmer, **Johads** in other parts).",
          "(3) **Rooftop Rainwater Harvesting & Tankas:** In Bikaner, Phalodi, and Barmer (Rajasthan), almost all houses had underground tanks or **tankas** built inside the main house or courtyard to store drinking water. Connected to sloping roofs via pipes; first rain was washed away to clean roof, subsequent rainwater stored.",
