          "**Technological Reforms (1960s–1970s):** The **Green Revolution** based on package technology (HYV seeds, irrigation, chemicals) and the **White Revolution (Operation Flood)** to increase milk production.",
          "**Comprehensive Land Development Programme (1980s–1990s):** Crop insurance against drought, flood, cyclone, fire, and disease; establishment of Grameen banks, cooperative societies to provide credit at low interest; **Kisan Credit Card (KCC)** and **Personal Accident Insurance Scheme (PAIS)**; special weather bulletins and agricultural programmes on radio and TV; Minimum Support Price (MSP) to prevent exploitation by middlemen.",
          "**Bhoodan – Gramdan Movement ('Bloodless Revolution'):** Started by **Vinoba Bhave**. In Pochampalli (Andhra Pradesh), landless villagers demanded land; **Shri Ram Chandra Reddy** offered 80 acres of his land to 80 landless villagers (known as **Bhoodan**). Later, some zamindars offered entire villages (**Gramdan**)."
